=== factory 
Plan work into tickets and run them on parallel coding-agent sessions

Usage:
  factory [command]

Available Commands:
  a2a          Serve the factory as an A2A agent
  add          Pin a file from a GitHub repository (MIT or Apache-2.0 only) in factory.lock
  audit        Read the audit log of what the factory did
  board        Open the terminal board
  browsercheck Run browser steps in headless Chrome and print one FACTORY_GATES line
  cancel       Cancel a ticket's running session
  checkpoint   Snapshot and restore the worktree around an agent session
  completion   Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  config       Read resolved configuration
  dashboard    Serve the read-only web view
  design       Make design edits to a JSX tree without a coding agent
  dispatch     Start a session for a ticket now
  doctor       Check the tools and settings the factory needs
  eval         Run the fixtures matrix and write a scorecard
  first-run    Audit this repo and show what the factory would fix, at no cost
  help         Help about any command
  init         Write .factory/factory.yaml from a tier preset
  logs         Print what a ticket's session is doing
  mcp          Serve the factory to Claude Code over stdio, or over HTTP with --http (MCP)
  packs        Inspect the packs pinned in factory.lock
  plan         Turn a goal, epic or spec into a ticket DAG; --approve files it
  policy       Check an action against a policy rules file (enterprise)
  queue        Show tickets ready to run and the merge queue
  repomap      Print a ranked, token-budgeted symbol map of the repository for a context pack
  report       Show tokens per merged PR, rework, human touches and cycle time (operator only)
  retry        Queue a new attempt for a ticket
  review       Run the check packs in .factory/checks against the uncommitted changes, edits returned as patches
  run          Run the factory; --headless streams one JSON event per line
  scim         Serve SCIM 2.0 Users and Groups for an identity provider (enterprise)
  serve        Run the factory loop as a service with /healthz, /readyz and /events
  shadow       Summarize what shadow mode would have dispatched
  smoke        Run the loop once against a sandbox GitHub repository with a fake agent
  status       Show the board, one row per slot
  steer        Send a message to a ticket's running session
  upgrade      Replace this binary with the latest factory release
  version      Print the factory version

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for factory

Use "factory [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== factory a2a
Serve the factory as an A2A agent

Usage:
  factory a2a [flags]

Flags:
      --addr string          listen address (default "127.0.0.1:8787")
      --audit-log string     file that gets one JSON line per call (default ".factory/a2a-audit.jsonl")
  -h, --help                 help for a2a
      --signing-key string   ECDSA P-256 PEM key that signs the agent card (a new key per start when empty)

=== factory add
Pin a file from a GitHub repository (MIT or Apache-2.0 only) in factory.lock

Usage:
  factory add <repo>#<path>[@ref] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help          help for add
      --kind string   skill, agent, workflow or check (default: from the path)
      --root string   repository root holding factory.lock and .factory/cache (default ".")

=== factory audit
Read the audit log of what the factory did

Usage:
  factory audit [command]

Available Commands:
  export      Print audit records from the last --since, as jsonl or csv

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for audit

Use "factory audit [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== factory audit export
Print audit records from the last --since, as jsonl or csv

Usage:
  factory audit export [flags]

Flags:
      --format string   jsonl or csv (default "jsonl")
  -h, --help            help for export
      --since string    how far back to read, such as 7d or 12h (default "7d")

=== factory board
Open the terminal board

Usage:
  factory board [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for board
      --operator        show tokens against budget on each card
      --replay string   play a recorded headless event stream (NDJSON) instead of a live fleet
      --speed float     replay speed: 10 plays ten times faster than recorded (default 1)

=== factory browsercheck
Run browser steps in headless Chrome and print one FACTORY_GATES line

